<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<grit-part>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_WIDEVINE_TITLE" desc="Optional protected media feature">Protected video and music (Widevine DRM)</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_WIDEVINE_SUMMARY" desc="Purpose of the optional DRM module">Plays media protected with Widevine. Krypton downloads Google's Widevine module to decrypt it.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_WIDEVINE_SHARED" desc="Network data shared by the optional DRM module">Downloads and update checks contact Google's update servers, revealing your IP address, operating system, browser and component versions. These requests can also update the certificate revocation list. During playback, the module contacts the media service's license server with information identifying this device to that service.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_WIDEVINE_RISK" desc="Privacy risk of the optional DRM module">Moderate. Widevine runs closed-source code in a sandbox to play protected media. Its behavior cannot be independently audited.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_WIDEVINE_OFF" desc="Behavior when the optional DRM module is disabled">Widevine-protected streams won't play. A previously downloaded module is neither loaded nor updated. This switch does not control other media protection systems.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_CAPTION_TITLE" desc="Optional local audio captions">Live Caption</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_CAPTION_SUMMARY" desc="How to start optional audio captions">Makes on-device audio captions available. After restarting, use Live Caption in the page context menu to start or stop captions.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_CAPTION_SHARED" desc="Data shared by optional local captions">Downloads the speech engine and each chosen language pack from Google's update servers. Requests reveal your IP address, operating system, browser and component versions, and can also refresh the certificate revocation list. Caption audio is processed on this device and is not sent to a server.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_CAPTION_RISK" desc="Privacy risk of the downloaded speech engine">Moderate. The downloaded speech engine runs closed-source code locally to produce captions. Its implementation cannot be independently audited. Translation and online speech models remain disabled.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_CAPTION_OFF" desc="Behavior when optional local captions are disabled">Live Caption is unavailable. Its speech engine and language packs are not updated for captioning. Previously downloaded caption models remain on disk.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_AUTOPLAY_TITLE" desc="Optional media autoplay allowlist">Let well-known media sites autoplay with sound</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_AUTOPLAY_SUMMARY" desc="Purpose of the downloaded autoplay list">Downloads a list of media sites that can play sound without a previous engagement history.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_AUTOPLAY_SHARED" desc="Data shared when fetching the autoplay list">Downloads and updates contact Google's component servers with your IP address, operating system, browser and component versions. These requests can also update the certificate revocation list.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_AUTOPLAY_RISK" desc="Privacy risk of the downloaded autoplay list">Low. The list changes which sites may autoplay with sound. Fetching it does not send browsing history.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_AUTOPLAY_OFF" desc="Behavior without the autoplay list">No downloaded preload list is used after restart. Ordinary per-site autoplay rules still apply.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_SEARCH_SUGGEST_TITLE" desc="Privacy toggle for remote address bar completions">Online search suggestions</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_SEARCH_SUGGEST_SUMMARY" desc="Purpose of online search suggestions">Shows suggestions from your default search engine as you type in the address bar. Off by default, as in Helium. Changes apply immediately.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_SEARCH_SUGGEST_SHARED" desc="Data sent by online search suggestions">Sends what you type in the address bar to your default search engine before you press Enter. Requests also reveal your IP address and may include search engine cookies. Suggestion images can load from image providers named by your search engine.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_SEARCH_SUGGEST_RISK" desc="Privacy risk of remote search suggestions">Moderate. Your search engine can receive incomplete searches and text you decide not to submit.</message>
  <message name="IDS_KRYPTON_PRIVACY_SEARCH_SUGGEST_OFF" desc="Behavior when remote suggestions are disabled">Online search suggestions are disabled. Local history, bookmarks and open tabs can still appear. Searches you submit still go to your search engine.</message>
</grit-part>
